  "body": "## What changed\n\n`assets/posts/fanuc-lathe.cps`, the C-axis live-tool G01 (`liveMove`):\n\n- **#1392, the floored word.** The cap is kept as its own value (`capF`, from #1395's prelude `rotaryFeedCap(Infinity, ...)`), and F goes through `capWord(v, cap)`. It returns `fm(v)` unless that word is over the cap; then it floors the word to the 0.1 step at or under the cap. No tolerance: flooring without one is only ever on the safe side.\n- **#1398, posted words.** The cap is measured between the words the control reads. X is read back from its rounded diameter word, Z origin-relative at 0.001, C at 0.001. This is the same rule as `rotaryFeed`'s `q()`/`org` for the mills (#1395). Before, it was measured on the unrounded points, and a short move that rounded longer could drive X/Z about 7% over the maximum feed. The planned F is still scaled by the raw composite length, so feeds away from their cap post byte-identically.\n- **F0 refused.** A word under the 0.1 mm/min step is refused by name and not written. One refusal covers a machine-rate cap that floors to F0, another a planned feed that small.\n- Merged upstream/main (#1395 rewrote `liveMove`). The merge keeps #1395's `rotaryFeedCap` and every #1395 refusal, as M3 resolved it in review.\n- Feeds away from their cap post byte-identically. **No recorded or golden program changed.**\n\n## How tested\n- `crates/post/tests/lathe_live_feed_cap.rs`, 8 tests:\n  - the 4 #1392 floor tests;\n  - `a_capped_move_is_judged_on_its_posted_words` (M3's probe, X20.001 -> X20.008, C30 -> C30.01; rates recomputed from the posted words stay within fmax and the C rate, for both the fmax-binding and the C-binding machine);\n  - `an_off_lattice_stream_is_judged_on_its_posted_words` (C, and Z with an off-step origin, rounding differently from the raw point);\n  - `a_cap_that_floors_under_the_f_step_is_refused_by_name` (M3's probe: C rate 0.05, a 90 degree turn, planned feed 50000);\n  - `an_uncapped_feed_under_the_f_step_is_refused_by_name`.\n- Mutation check: 13 mutants, every one RED, and GREEN once restored. The table is in the review-fix PR comment.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-post`: 433 passed, 0 failed.\n- App suites `rotary_feed_cap`, `c_axis_fixture`, `c_axis_live` (golden), `c_axis_unwind`, `program_units`, `recorded_post_streams`, `conformance`, `lathe_post`, `lathe_post_inch`, `lathe_post_css`, `lathe_post_g76`: all green.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` on the final head: green on 6a58d35b (post suites 3 s incl. lathe_live_feed_cap, 27 app suites 82 s, 0 failed)\n\n## Not exercised\n- Inch C sections: fanuc-lathe refuses them, so there is no inch path. The read-back still converts if that ever changes.\n- A real control. How a Fanuc lathe handles the X-diameter rate needs a desk review or a tester.\n\nDecision record: `docs/decisions/1392-floor-capped-feed.md` (review note dated 2026-11-13).\n\nFork synced at v0.18.0; merged upstream/main 38699549.\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nChangelog: fanuc-lathe: a C-axis live-tool feed is capped on the words it posts and floored, never rounded, over the machine's feed or C rate; a feed that would post F0 is refused by name (#1392, #1398)\n\nFixes #1392\nFixes #1398\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
